  "steps": [
    "Preheat oven to 500°F. Line a baking sheet with foil. Reserve 4 tomatillos raw; place remaining halved tomatillos and the tomato cut-side down on the sheet. Roast until lightly charred, about 20 minutes.",
    "In a food processor, add the roasted tomatillos and tomato, reserved raw tomatillos, jalapeños (start with half if unsure), red onion, garlic, cilantro, cumin, and oregano. Pulse until mostly smooth with some texture.",
    "Stir in lemon and lime juices. Season to taste with salt and pepper (about 1 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp pepper to start). Adjust heat by adding more jalapeño or seeds as desired. Serve chilled or at room temperature."
